Maintainer: @@VENDOR@@ <maintainers@astraos.invalid>
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://astraos.invalid
Depends: astraos-base (>= @@VERSION@@), python3 (>= 3.11), python3-gi, python3-gi-cairo, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, coreutils, procps
Recommends: gir1.2-vte-3.91, fonts-dejavu-core
Description: AstraOS full-screen system dashboard
 The AstraOS HUD is the session's overview surface: one full-screen window that
 shows what the machine is doing at a glance. It is drawn with GTK 3 and Cairo
 and reads its numbers straight from /proc and /sys, with no third-party Python
 package - there is no psutil in the image.
 .
  * CPU, per-core load, memory, swap, load average and the top processes
  * per-interface network traffic, latency and a rolling traffic graph
  * mounted filesystems and their usage, disk I/O and temperatures
  * the clock, uptime and battery state, in the AstraOS palette
 .
 It is started by hand or from its launcher. It is not a system service, it
 registers no autostart entry, and nothing starts it at boot, so it costs the
 session nothing until it is asked for.
 .
 A value that cannot be measured - no battery, no thermal zone, a counter with
 only one sample - is shown as a dash rather than invented, so a number on screen
 is always something the kernel actually reported. The embedded terminal appears
 only when gir1.2-vte-3.91 is installed; without it the HUD starts anyway and
 says so instead of failing.
